  "body": "What happens: `cargo xtask gate release` runs its steps one after the other. The run of the v0.20.0 cut took more than 90 minutes on one machine. The maintainer asked for parallel lanes, 2026-11-14: \"like.. 4 gate runners at a time then.\"\n\nWanted:\n- The gate builds the test binaries once, then runs independent lanes at the same time, with a limit of 4 lanes.\n- The debug lanes and the release lanes run side by side (they use different `target/` subdirectories).\n- The suites with a time limit (the 30 s and 90 s watchdogs) and the UI suites that open windows run alone, so that load does not make them fail.\n- Optional: split the lanes across the self-hosted runners `uma` and `m3`.\n- `cargo xtask release` on Windows refuses with \"Cargo.lock changed beyond version lines\" when the only difference is CRLF line endings. Correct that comparison.\n\nDone means: a release-tier run on one machine reports each lane with its own log and wall time, the total wall time is measured against the serial run, and `xtask` unit tests pin the lane plan.\n",
